== (1) exact pseudo-rotation of the naive Dirac operator (open box, compact support) ==
plane (3,0) spin-term sign +1: max |[Dirac, L_w] psi| = 5.590e+00
plane (3,0) spin-term sign -1: max |[Dirac, L_w] psi| = 0.000e+00
plane (0,1) spin-term sign +1: max |[Dirac, L_w] psi| = 5.590e+00
plane (0,1) spin-term sign -1: max |[Dirac, L_w] psi| = 0.000e+00
plane (2,3) spin-term sign +1: max |[Dirac, L_w] psi| = 5.858e+00
plane (2,3) spin-term sign -1: max |[Dirac, L_w] psi| = 0.000e+00
(the sign that gives 0 is the exact symmetry; delta psi = L psi, delta psibar = -psibar L)

== (2) spin diagonalisation: shifts used by L map to scalar phases ==
max deviation from scalar phase over all parity classes, diagonal and two-step shifts: 0.0
=> F (two-step) and Sigma (diagonal shifts x gamma_a gamma_b) act within one staggered component:
   the staggered fermion inherits exact pseudo-translations and pseudo-rotations.

== (3) Killing closure for the fermion ==
m2=0.25: best translation fit of [L_w, F_r] on the shell: relative residual min/max = 0.542/0.978
m2=1.0: best translation fit of [L_w, F_r] on the shell: relative residual min/max = 0.398/0.976

== (4) Gordon identity on the complex shell (symmetric-stress criterion) ==
max |v g_mu u - (-i sin k_mu / m) v u| / |v u| = 4.17e-15
=> zero-momentum on-shell current of translation f: ~ (v dD/dk_mu u) f_nu ~ sin k_mu cos k_mu f_nu;
   symmetric in (mu,nu) iff f_nu ~ sin 2k_nu: the staggered two-step pseudo-momentum (L1's spectrum).
